ARFLAGS is where builds of GNU Make 4.4.1 stop agreeing. The released source
answers `-rv` under `.POSIX:` and so does Fedora's build and Arch's; Debian's
make-dfsg answers `-rvU`, asking `ar` not to write the deterministic archive it
would otherwise write. The recording is the released source's, so this case
fails first on a host whose `make` is Debian's. See docs/make-oracle-divergences.md.
